          %h3#DifferentiationLayerMod Model Layer
          %p We discuss
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#DifferentiationOfSmoothFunctionsAndDifferentialForms"} Differentiation of smooth functions and differential forms
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    first just
                    %em
                      %a{:href => "#DifferentiationOnCoordinatePatches"} on coordinate patches
                %li
                  %p
                    and then
                    = succeed "." do
                      %em
                        %a{:href => "#DifferentiationOnSmoothSpaces"} on general smooth spaces
          %p
            By considering
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+products"} fiber products
            of smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+spaces"} mapping spaces
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+spaces"} discrete spaces
            of boundary configurations, we obtain from this the differentiation theory called
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#VariationalCalculus"} Variational calculus
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    with the notion of
                    %em
                      %a{:href => "#SmoothFunctionals"} Smooth functional
                %li
                  %p
                    and
                    %em
                      %a{:href => "#FunctionalDerivative"} Variational derivative
                    of smooth functionals.
                %li
                  %p
                    The central class of examples of this of interest in physics is the variation of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functionals"} action functionals
                    that yields the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+equations"} Euler-Lagrange
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
                    in
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theory"} classical field theory
                    = succeed "." do
                      %em
                        %a{:href => "#EulerLagrangeEquations"} Euler-Lagrange equations
          %h4#DifferentiationOfSmoothFunctionsAndDifferentialForms Differentiation of smooth functions and differential forms
          %h5#DifferentiationOnCoordinatePatches Differentiation on coordinate patches
          %p
            By definition to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}
            is associated its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivative"} derivative
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f' \colon \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}
            are associated its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+derivatives"} partial derivatives
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∂
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\frac{\partial f}{\partial x^i} \colon \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}
          %p
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi i
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \leq i \leq n
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+differential"} de Rham differential
            collects all partial derivatives of a function into a single
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+1-form"} differential 1-form
          #DeRhamDifferentialOn1Forms.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+differential"} de Rham differential
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{d} \colon C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n) \to \Omega^1(\mathbb{R}^n)
            %p
              which takes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
              to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
                    %mi f
                    %mo ≔
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi n
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi i
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{d}f \coloneqq \sum_{i = 1}^n \frac{\partial f}{\partial x^i} \mathbf{d} x^i
                    \\,.
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^i \colon \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}
              one of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate"} coordinate
              functions, the de Rham differential
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{d} x^i
              indeed coincides with the basis element of the same name according to def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Differential1FormsOnCartesianSpaces"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi j
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi i
                              %mo =
                              %mi j
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi otherwise
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\frac{\partial x^i}{\partial x^{j}} =
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    1 &amp; | i = j
                    \\\
                    0 &amp; | otherwise
                    }
                    \\right.
                    \\,.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The de Rham differentials
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{d} \colon C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n) \to \Omega^1(\mathbb{R}^n)
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              are compatible with
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+differential+forms"} pullback of differential 1-forms
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PullbackOfDifferential1FormsOnCartesianSpaces"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mover
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon \mathbb{R}^{\tilde k} \to \mathbb{R}^{k}
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
